# The standing false approvals by channel (the reviewer's reading after run 38; the reader corrected November 6, 2026 — the panel read from the case's challenge record with its kind, a paid appeal its own channel): the chain's finals on seeds 21–40, the direct (results/redteam/stability/learned-rev-careful-290-own/direct/models/direct-online-10.pt) and head alone (results/redteam/stability/learned-rev-careful-290-own/wm/models/wm-online-10.pt), the hand beside. A standing false approval: a real root (not a plant, not the state's delivery) vested with its work unfulfilled. Channels: its audit seat confirmed it (a member's or the state's — a troop at the audit seat), it was audited and rejected yet vested (the third seat or a ruling), it was disputed by its requester and the panel confirmed it (no audit review: §4 discharges the obligation at the dispute's settlement; split by whether a member sat on the panel or the state's reviewers alone did), its actor appealed its N and the panel sided with the appellant — a paid appeal (the same split), or it was never audited (no audit review, no challenge: the roll never sent it). `rolled but never seated` counts never-audited cases with an obligation recorded (should be 0: a vested case has no standing obligation).

